{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE OF COMPLETION — merged.\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2144 (LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, submitted; merged as f403b97e4c on main).\n\nWhat landed: acli_cli_ops.add_comment now returns _parse_comment_created(result.stdout) — a dict WITHOUT envelope markers (results/successCount) passes through verbatim (DC/REST comment resource); the Cloud batch envelope normalizes to {\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <parsed>} so results[].id (a WORK ITEM key) can never be mistaken for a comment id; any other shape raises loudly. _record_comment_id docstring updated to the normalized contract.\n\nACs:\n- AC1 (normalizer, recorded-envelope fixtures): DONE — tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py: ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE + live-recorded ACLI_FAILURE_ENVELOPE (acli 1.3.19-stable, provenance noted in file); success-envelope-normalized, resource-passthrough, unrecognized-raises, failure-envelope-raises-AcliMutationError. 8 passed.\n- AC2 (no consumer sees the raw envelope): DONE — the only production consumer chain (_record_comment_id) exercised via the seam-crossing suite (change 2145).\n- AC3 (audit of other raw --json passthroughs): DONE — recorded in prior comment: acli.update_issue raw passthrough is latent-only (no consumer reads fields).\n\nGates: targeted 30 passed + apply/diffing/mutate suites 963 passed; make lint (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); make typecheck clean. Also fixed the two suite-level guards the new symbol tripped in CI (rate-limit sweep NON-MUTATING classification; timeout-test payload expectation) — in the same change, patchset 2."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787465539808671001,"uuid":"78aec243-458b-4639-9e2f-0db5ceb6e804"}